IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oas-core`

-- Old Age Security Act (R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9) -- from the seat of the person applying for, or receiving, an Old Age
-- Security benefit: the pension, the Guaranteed Income Supplement, the Allowance or the Allowance for the Survivor.
-- "Can I get the pension? How much? How much GIS? Can my spouse or I get the Allowance?" Facts are ones that person
-- can state. The rules are in oas-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no
-- rule.
--
-- FIGURES. The indexed amounts for the payment quarter are not deposited. Each amount question asks for them: they are
-- published every quarter by Employment and Social Development Canada (Service Canada). Unofficial; not an official
-- version. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Old Age Security -- the applicant's questions`

DECLARE `OAS amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no pension` HAS `because` IS A `Pension eligibility`
    `no allowance` HAS `because` IS AN `Allowance eligibility`
    `no supplement this month (s 11(7))`

GIVEN `full monthly pension` IS A NUMBER, `maximum single` IS A NUMBER, `maximum couple` IS A NUMBER, `survivor equivalent` IS A NUMBER, `top-up 50` IS A NUMBER, `top-up 35` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `OAS quarter figures`
`the quarter's figures from my answers` `full monthly pension` `maximum single` `maximum couple` `survivor equivalent` `top-up 50` `top-up 35` MEANS
    `OAS quarter figures` WITH
        `full monthly pension`                      IS `full monthly pension`
        `maximum supplement, single rate`           IS `maximum single`
        `maximum supplement, pensioner couple rate` IS `maximum couple`
        `supplement equivalent for the survivor`    IS `survivor equivalent`
        `top-up figure A of $50`                    IS `top-up 50`
        `top-up figure A of $35`                    IS `top-up 35`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER, `resident day before` IS A BOOLEAN, `legal` IS A BOOLEAN, `1977` IS A BOOLEAN, `ten years` IS A BOOLEAN, `present before` IS A NUMBER, `absent during` IS A NUMBER, `last year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Pension applicant`
`the pension applicant from my answers` `age` `years` `resident day before` `legal` `1977` `ten years` `present before` `absent during` `last year` MEANS
    `Pension applicant` WITH
        `age`                                                                 IS `age`
        `years resided in Canada after 18 and before approval`                IS `years`
        `resided in Canada on the day before approval`                        IS `resident day before`
        `citizen or legally resident on the day before approval, or on the day before ceasing to reside in Canada` IS `legal`
        `was 25 or older on 1 July 1977 and resided in Canada then, or had resided after 18, or held an immigration visa` IS `1977`
        `resided in Canada for the 10 years immediately before approval`      IS `ten years`
        `years present in Canada after 18 and before those 10 years`          IS `present before`
        `years absent from Canada during those 10 years`                      IS `absent during`
        `resided in Canada for the year immediately before approval`          IS `last year`

§§ `Part I -- my Old Age Security pension`

@export Can I be paid an Old Age Security pension, full or partial, and in how many fortieths (ss 3 and 4)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when your pension application is (or would be) approved
      `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` IS A NUMBER @desc The total years you have lived in Canada (made your home and ordinarily lived here) since your 18th birthday, up to approval; temporary absences of up to a year and absences to study count as residence
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before your application is approved
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada on the day before approval, or were on the day before you stopped living in Canada
      `I was 25 or older on 1 July 1977 with ties to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether on 1 July 1977 you were 25 or older and lived in Canada, or had lived in Canada at some time after 18, or held a valid immigration visa (answer no if born after 1 July 1952)
      `I lived in Canada for the last 10 years before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived in Canada for the whole of the 10 years immediately before approval
      `years present in Canada after 18 before those 10 years` IS A NUMBER @desc Years you were physically in Canada after turning 18 and before those last 10 years (0 if you answered yes above)
      `years absent from Canada during those 10 years` IS A NUMBER @desc Years you were away from Canada during the last 10 years before approval (0 if none)
      `I lived in Canada for the year before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lived in Canada for at least the whole year immediately before approval
GIVETH A `Pension eligibility`
`Can I get an OAS pension` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I was 25 or older on 1 July 1977 with ties to Canada` `I lived in Canada for the last 10 years before approval` `years present in Canada after 18 before those 10 years` `years absent from Canada during those 10 years` `I lived in Canada for the year before approval` MEANS
    `the pension the applicant may be paid`
        (`the pension applicant from my answers` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I was 25 or older on 1 July 1977 with ties to Canada` `I lived in Canada for the last 10 years before approval` `years present in Canada after 18 before those 10 years` `years absent from Canada during those 10 years` `I lived in Canada for the year before approval`)

@export How much is my monthly Old Age Security pension, with any increase for deferring it and the 10% from age 75 (ss 3(3), 7(5), 7.1)?
GIVEN `the full monthly pension this quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The full monthly OAS pension for the payment quarter as published by Service Canada for people aged 65 to 74, in Canadian dollars (before any deferral increase)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when your pension application is (or would be) approved
      `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` IS A NUMBER @desc The total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday, up to approval
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before your application is approved
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada on the day before approval, or were on the day before you stopped living in Canada
      `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I first qualified` IS A NUMBER @desc The total years you had lived in Canada since 18 when you first qualified for a pension (usually at 65)
      `months from the month after I qualified to the month of approval` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months you put off your pension: counted from the month after you first qualified to the month your application is approved (0 if you took it at once)
      `months from the month after I qualified to the month I turn 70` IS A NUMBER @desc Months from the month after you first qualified to the month of your 70th birthday (60 if you qualified at 65)
      `months in that time I was abroad over six months or in prison` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the deferral months, how many your pension would have been suspended for (outside Canada after six months without 20 years' residence, or serving a federal or long provincial sentence)
      `I turned 75 before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this month is after the month of your 75th birthday
GIVETH AN `OAS amount answer`
`How much is my OAS pension` `the full monthly pension this quarter` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I first qualified` `months from the month after I qualified to the month of approval` `months from the month after I qualified to the month I turn 70` `months in that time I was abroad over six months or in prison` `I turned 75 before this month` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `the pension the applicant may be paid` (`the pension applicant from my answers` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since turning 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE)
        `figures` MEANS `the quarter's figures from my answers` `the full monthly pension this quarter` 0 0 0 0 0
        `facts` MEANS `Pension amount facts` WITH
                        `eligibility`                                            IS `eligibility`
                        `whole years of residence after 18 when first qualified` IS FLOOR `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I first qualified`
                        `qualified for a full pension when first qualified`      IS `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I first qualified` AT LEAST 40
                        `deferral`                                               IS `Deferral facts` WITH
                                                                                      `months from the month after qualifying to the month of approval` IS `months from the month after I qualified to the month of approval`
                                                                                      `months from the month after qualifying to the month of turning 70` IS `months from the month after I qualified to the month I turn 70`
                                                                                      `of those months, months the pension would have been suspended or not paid` IS `months in that time I was abroad over six months or in prison`
                        `past the month of turning 75`                           IS `I turned 75 before this month`
    IN CONSIDER `the monthly pension` `figures` `facts`
       WHEN JUST `x` THEN `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is` `x`
       WHEN NOTHING THEN `no pension` `eligibility`

@export Will my Old Age Security pension be suspended while I am outside Canada (s 9)?
GIVEN `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I left` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you had lived in Canada since your 18th birthday when you left Canada (or stopped living here)
      `full months I have been away after the month I left` IS A NUMBER @desc Number of whole months you have been outside Canada, not counting the month you left
GIVETH AN `Absence answer`
`Will my OAS pension stop while I am abroad` `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I left` `full months I have been away after the month I left` MEANS
    `the effect of absence from Canada` `years I had lived in Canada since 18 when I left` `full months I have been away after the month I left`

§§ `Part II -- the Guaranteed Income Supplement`

@export What is my income for the Guaranteed Income Supplement and the allowances, for a calendar year (s 2 "income")?
GIVEN `my income under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total (net) income for the year as computed under the Income Tax Act (line 23600 of your return), in Canadian dollars
      `my employment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income from employment for the year, before deductions
      `my EI premiums` IS A NUMBER @desc Employment Insurance premiums you paid as an employee in the year
      `my CPP contributions as an employee` IS A NUMBER @desc Canada (or Quebec) Pension Plan contributions you paid as an employee in the year
      `my self-employment earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net self-employment earnings for the year (0 if none)
      `my CPP contributions on self-employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Canada (or Quebec) Pension Plan contributions you paid on self-employment earnings
      `my EI special benefits premiums as self-employed` IS A NUMBER @desc Employment Insurance premiums you paid as a self-employed person under Part VII.1 (0 if none)
      `OAS benefits in my income` IS A NUMBER @desc Old Age Security pension, supplement or allowance (and similar provincial payments) included in your income for the year
      `CPP death benefit in my income` IS A NUMBER @desc Any CPP or QPP death benefit included in your income for the year
      `means-tested social assistance in my income` IS A NUMBER @desc Means-tested social assistance (such as provincial welfare) included in your income for the year
      `other adjustments to deduct` IS A NUMBER @desc Anything else the Act deducts: pandemic benefits (CERB, CRB, Worker Lockdown Benefit, EI Part VIII.4), three times any unused dividend tax credit, and amounts included under Income Tax Act 56(1)(q.1) or 56(6), less amounts deductible under 60(y) or (z) (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my income for the GIS` `my income under the Income Tax Act` `my employment income` `my EI premiums` `my CPP contributions as an employee` `my self-employment earnings` `my CPP contributions on self-employment` `my EI special benefits premiums as self-employed` `OAS benefits in my income` `CPP death benefit in my income` `means-tested social assistance in my income` `other adjustments to deduct` MEANS
    `income under s 2`
        (`Income facts` WITH
            `income for the year under the Income Tax Act`             IS `my income under the Income Tax Act`
            `income from office or employment`                         IS `my employment income`
            `EI employee's premiums paid`                              IS `my EI premiums`
            `CPP employee's contributions paid`                        IS `my CPP contributions as an employee`
            `self-employment earnings`                                 IS `my self-employment earnings`
            `CPP contributions on self-employment earnings`            IS `my CPP contributions on self-employment`
            `EI Part VII.1 premiums paid`                              IS `my EI special benefits premiums as self-employed`
            `benefits under this Act included in income`               IS `OAS benefits in my income`
            `CPP death benefit included in income`                     IS `CPP death benefit in my income`
            `means-tested social assistance included in income`        IS `means-tested social assistance in my income`
            `pandemic benefits listed in paragraph (c.1)`              IS `other adjustments to deduct`
            `s 121 dividend credit in excess of tax otherwise payable` IS 0
            `amounts included under ITA 56(1)(q.1) or 56(6)`           IS 0
            `amounts deductible under ITA 60(y) or (z)`                IS 0)

@export How much Guaranteed Income Supplement can I get this month (ss 11(7), 12, 12.1, 22(2), 22(6), 22.1(1))?
GIVEN `the full monthly pension this quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The full monthly OAS pension for the payment quarter, as published by Service Canada (the amount for ages 65 to 74), in Canadian dollars
      `the maximum GIS for a single pensioner, before the top-up` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory maximum supplement for this quarter for a pensioner without a pensioner spouse (s 12(1)(a) as indexed), without the s 12.1 top-up
      `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory maximum supplement for this quarter for a pensioner whose spouse or partner is also a pensioner (s 12(1)(b)(ii) as indexed)
      `the $50 top-up figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed amount for this quarter that the Act started at $50 plus $78.92 (s 12.1(1) "A")
      `the $35 top-up figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed amount for this quarter that the Act started at $35 (s 12.1(2)(b) "A")
      `my situation` IS A `Marital case` @desc One of: no spouse or common-law partner; a spouse or partner who is not a pensioner and gets no allowance; a spouse or partner who is a pensioner; a spouse or partner who gets the allowance
      `my income last year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the last calendar year as the Act counts it (see the income question)
      `my spouse's or partner's income last year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your spouse's or common-law partner's income for the last calendar year as the Act counts it (0 if none, or no spouse)
      `my monthly OAS pension, without deferral increase` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly OAS pension this month, leaving out any increase for having deferred it (include the 10% from 75)
      `years I have lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday
      `years my spouse or partner has lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years your spouse or partner has lived in Canada since 18 (any number of 10 or more if not relevant)
      `I turned 75 before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this month is after the month of your 75th birthday
      `no pension can be paid to me this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your OAS pension is not payable this month (for example, suspended or in a federal prison)
      `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been outside Canada (or not living here) for six full months before this month
      `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an immigration sponsor's undertaking for you is in effect this month (and no sponsor event under the Regulations has occurred)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much GIS can I get` `the full monthly pension this quarter` `the maximum GIS for a single pensioner, before the top-up` `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` `the $50 top-up figure` `the $35 top-up figure` `my situation` `my income last year` `my spouse's or partner's income last year` `my monthly OAS pension, without deferral increase` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `years my spouse or partner has lived in Canada since 18` `I turned 75 before this month` `no pension can be paid to me this month` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` MEANS
    `the monthly supplement`
        (`the quarter's figures from my answers` `the full monthly pension this quarter` `the maximum GIS for a single pensioner, before the top-up` `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` 0 `the $50 top-up figure` `the $35 top-up figure`)
        (`Supplement facts` WITH
            `marital case`                                         IS `my situation`
            `the pensioner's income for the base calendar year`    IS `my income last year`
            `the spouse's or partner's income for the base calendar year` IS `my spouse's or partner's income last year`
            `the pensioner's monthly pension, without deferral increase` IS `my monthly OAS pension, without deferral increase`
            `the pensioner's years of residence after 18`          IS `years I have lived in Canada since 18`
            `the spouse's or partner's years of residence after 18` IS `years my spouse or partner has lived in Canada since 18`
            `past the month of turning 75`                         IS `I turned 75 before this month`
            `no pension may be paid for the month`                 IS `no pension can be paid to me this month`
            `outside Canada for six consecutive months before this month` IS `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month`
            `a sponsorship undertaking is in effect`               IS `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect`)

§§ `Part III -- the Allowance (situation: you are 60 to 64 and your spouse or partner is an OAS pensioner)`

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER, `resident day before` IS A BOOLEAN, `legal` IS A BOOLEAN, `abroad` IS A BOOLEAN, `sponsored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Allowance applicant`
`the allowance applicant from my answers` `age` `years` `resident day before` `legal` `abroad` `sponsored` MEANS
    `Allowance applicant` WITH
        `age`                                                       IS `age`
        `years resided in Canada after 18 and before approval`      IS `years`
        `resided in Canada on the day before approval`              IS `resident day before`
        `citizen or legally resident`                               IS `legal`
        `outside Canada for six consecutive months before this month` IS `abroad`
        `a sponsorship undertaking is in effect`                    IS `sponsored`

@export Can I get the Allowance as the spouse or common-law partner of an OAS pensioner (s 19)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `years I have lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday, up to approval
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before approval
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada
      `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been outside Canada for six full months before this month
      `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an immigration sponsor's undertaking for you is in effect this month
      `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are living with your pensioner spouse or partner, or separated no more than three months before this month
      `the pensioner gets the GIS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or partner, the pensioner, can be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for the month
GIVETH AN `Allowance eligibility`
`Can I get the Allowance` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` `the pensioner gets the GIS` MEANS
    `the s 19 allowance eligibility`
        (`the allowance applicant from my answers` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect`)
        `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` `the pensioner gets the GIS`

@export How much Allowance can I get this month as the spouse or partner of an OAS pensioner (ss 22(3), 22.1(2); Regulations s 6)?
GIVEN `the full monthly pension this quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The full monthly OAS pension for the payment quarter (the amount for ages 65 to 74), in Canadian dollars
      `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory maximum supplement for this quarter for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner (s 12(1)(b)(ii) as indexed, the "supplement equivalent")
      `the $35 top-up figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed amount for this quarter that the Act started at $35 (s 22.1(2) "A")
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `years I have lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before approval
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada
      `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been outside Canada for six full months before this month
      `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an immigration sponsor's undertaking for you is in effect this month
      `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are living with your pensioner spouse or partner, or separated no more than three months before this month
      `the pensioner gets the GIS` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pensioner can be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for the month
      `our combined income last year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income plus the pensioner's income for the last calendar year, as the Act counts income
GIVETH AN `OAS amount answer`
`How much Allowance can I get` `the full monthly pension this quarter` `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` `the $35 top-up figure` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` `the pensioner gets the GIS` `our combined income last year` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `Can I get the Allowance` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `I live with the pensioner or separated three months ago or less` `the pensioner gets the GIS`
        `figures` MEANS `the quarter's figures from my answers` `the full monthly pension this quarter` 0 `the maximum GIS for a pensioner whose spouse is a pensioner` 0 0 `the $35 top-up figure`
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `eligible for the allowance (s 19)` THEN
            `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is`
                (`with the $2 minimum` ((`the s 22(3) allowance` `figures` `our combined income last year` `years I have lived in Canada since 18`) PLUS (`the s 22.1(1) or (2) top-up` `figures` `our combined income last year` `years I have lived in Canada since 18`)))
       OTHERWISE `no allowance` `eligibility`

§§ `Part III -- the Allowance for the Survivor (situation: your spouse or partner has died and you are 60 to 64)`

@export Can I get the Allowance for the Survivor (ss 2, 21, 21.1)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `years I have lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday, up to approval
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before approval
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada
      `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been outside Canada for six full months before this month
      `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an immigration sponsor's undertaking for you is in effect this month
      `my spouse or partner has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or common-law partner has died
      `I have had a new spouse or partner since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have married or become the common-law partner of someone else since that death
      `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of the murder or manslaughter of that spouse or partner (s 21.1)
GIVETH AN `Allowance eligibility`
`Can I get the Allowance for the Survivor` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `my spouse or partner has died` `I have had a new spouse or partner since` `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner` MEANS
    `the s 21 allowance eligibility`
        (`the allowance applicant from my answers` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect`)
        `my spouse or partner has died` `I have had a new spouse or partner since` `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner`

@export How much Allowance for the Survivor can I get this month (ss 22(4), 22.1(3); Regulations s 6)?
GIVEN `the full monthly pension this quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The full monthly OAS pension for the payment quarter (the amount for ages 65 to 74), in Canadian dollars
      `the supplement equivalent for the survivor` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed "supplement equivalent for the survivor" for this quarter (s 22(4.1)-(4.4))
      `the $50 top-up figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexed amount for this quarter that the Act started at $50 plus $78.92 (s 22.1(3) "A")
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `years I have lived in Canada since 18` IS A NUMBER @desc Total years you have lived in Canada since your 18th birthday
      `I lived in Canada the day before approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were living in Canada on the day before approval
      `I am a citizen or legal resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a Canadian citizen or legally resident in Canada
      `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been outside Canada for six full months before this month
      `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an immigration sponsor's undertaking for you is in effect this month
      `my spouse or partner has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or common-law partner has died
      `I have had a new spouse or partner since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have married or become the common-law partner of someone else since that death
      `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of the murder or manslaughter of that spouse or partner
      `my income last year` IS A NUMBER @desc Your income for the last calendar year, as the Act counts income
GIVETH AN `OAS amount answer`
`How much Allowance for the Survivor can I get` `the full monthly pension this quarter` `the supplement equivalent for the survivor` `the $50 top-up figure` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `my spouse or partner has died` `I have had a new spouse or partner since` `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner` `my income last year` MEANS
    LET `eligibility` MEANS `Can I get the Allowance for the Survivor` `my age` `years I have lived in Canada since 18` `I lived in Canada the day before approval` `I am a citizen or legal resident` `I have been outside Canada for six months before this month` `a sponsorship undertaking for me is in effect` `my spouse or partner has died` `I have had a new spouse or partner since` `I was convicted of killing my spouse or partner`
        `figures` MEANS `the quarter's figures from my answers` `the full monthly pension this quarter` 0 0 `the supplement equivalent for the survivor` `the $50 top-up figure` 0
    IN CONSIDER `eligibility`
       WHEN `eligible for the allowance for the survivor (s 21)` THEN
            `the amount, in Canadian dollars a month, is` (`the allowance for the survivor` `figures` `my income last year` `years I have lived in Canada since 18`)
       OTHERWISE `no allowance` `eligibility`
